// // SPRITES ORDERING // //

(note this isnt a spriting GUIDE, that is coming soon!)

so this is how sprites are ordered:

yourmod/sprites/
              .../units/any(your directories!)
              .../effect/any(your directiories!)
              ...blocks/
                     ...distribution/ <- ducts, conveyors, routers, junctions, rest of item distribution usually go in here
                     ...production/ <- crafters, attribute crafters, heat crafters, etc usually go in here
                     ...walls/ <- walls go in here
                     ...effect(or defense)/ <- menders, overdrive projectors, build towers, regen projectors, force projectors, etc usually go in here
                     ...storage/ <- cores and vaults usually go in here
                     ...liquid/ <- conduits, liquid routers, liquid bridges, pumps, rest of liquid distribution usually go in here
                     ...power/ <- power nodes, beam nodes, batteries, diodes, consume generators, impact reactors, and power producing blocks usually go in here
                     ...drills/ <- wall drills, floor drills, cliff crushers, oil extractors usually go in here
                     ...turrets/ <- power turrets, item turrets, point defense turrets, etc often go in here
                     ...units/ <- Unit producing blocks go in here, stuff like unit factories, unit assemblies, reconstructors, repair points, repair fields
                     ...logic/ <- Logic processors, messages, and memory cells go in here
                     ...environment/any(your directories!) <- Environmental blocks go here, and only in here, the game doesnt load them(if im not mistaken)
            
Thats how sprites are structured
Although take the [this block/unit goes in here] stuff with a grain of salt
you can still put stuff like cores in walls, etc

plus you can make your own directories within stuff like turrets, environment, liquid, etc

(although do correct me if i am wrong!)
